WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.270
Yosemite National Park, 2025: almost
four and a half million visits.

2
00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:08.950
They are concentrated in a few valleys.

3
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:13.570
The park also holds 774
park service buildings.

4
00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:18.970
Yet the Wilderness Act of 1964 describes
wilderness as land where man himself

5
00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:21.810
is a visitor who does not remain.

6
00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:24.410
And wilderness covers most of the park.

7
00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:28.410
So how can crowds and legal
wilderness both work in one park?

8
00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:30.730
Is the wilderness closed?

9
00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:32.590
Are visitor numbers falling?

10
00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:35.770
In this mission, you'll weigh
threats to glaciated uplands,

11
00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:38.370
from avalanches to tourism.

12
00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:40.110
Then you'll meet Yosemite's stakeholders,

13
00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:45.770
and weigh how the park is managed,
from strict protection to multiple use.

14
00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:51.230
Your mission: explain how Yosemite can
keep both its crowds and its wilderness.
